      "heading": "2. Mathematical Formulation & Step-by-Step Derivation",
      "body": "$$\nW' = W_0 + \\Delta W = W_0 + \\frac{\\alpha}{r} B A\n$$\n\n**Derivation Steps:**\n1. A full weight matrix W_0 \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d \\times k} has d \\times k parameters (e.g., 4096 \\times 4096 = 16.7M).\n2. Constrain the update \\Delta W = B A where rank r \\ll \\min(d, k) (e.g., r = 16).\n3. Total trainable parameters become r(d + k) = 16(4096 + 4096) = 131,072 (<1% of full fine-tuning)."
