      "explanation": "Exam Analysis: Using a polar protic solvent (like water or ethanol) when attempting an SN2 reaction cages the anionic nucleophile in hydrogen bonds, drastically slowing SN2 and favoring SN1/E1 pathways. Worked reference: Reacting (R)-2-bromobutane with NaCN in DMSO (polar aprotic) proceeds via SN2 to yield pure (S)-2-cyanobutane with 100% inversion of stereochemistry."
